{
  "slug": "waves-exovian",
  "name": "Waves Exovian",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Waves is a product development framework that turns ideas into production software through a structured sequence of AI-driven artifacts. It provides the AI agent with persistent memory, project awareness, and a clear methodology — so every session starts informed, every task traces to a purpose, and every decision is recorded.\n\nThe framework guides the complete lifecycle: validate the idea (feasibility analysis with Monte Carlo and Bayesian projections and kill criteria), distill findings into validated facts (foundation), define what the product is and why it exists (blueprint with capabilities, flows, rules, and success metrics), plan delivery in organic cycles called waves (roadmaps with phases and milestones), track implementation per task (logbooks with objectives, scope, and completion guides), execute code aligned with project rules and business intent (objectives-implement), and document what was accomplished (resolutions).\n\nEach artifact feeds the next. Each session picks up where the last one left off. The agent reads the blueprint before writing code, follows extracted coding rules, alerts when work doesn't align with the product definition, and preserves context so nothing is lost between sessions.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, **21 agents**, **27 commands** and **5 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `waves-protocol` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"initialize a project\", \"create a manifest\", \"create rules\",…)\n- **Agents** (21): `antipattern-detector` (Educational agent that identifies antipatterns and bad practices in project code for each layer and framework), `architecture-detective` (Detects architectural layers, patterns, and boundaries across the codebase), `change-analyzer` (Pipeline agent that combines autogen detection, manifest change analysis, and timestamp-based analysis), `code-auditor` (Audits code changes against project rules to verify compliance), `code-implementer` (Implements code for specific objectives following project rules, patterns, and completion guides), `convention-detector` (Detects naming and coding conventions across a target layer), `dependency-auditor` (Audits dependencies, package managers, and build tools to categorize dependencies, detect risks (unlocked versions, duplicates, orphaned deps), and…), `entry-point-analyzer` (Identifies application entry points (frontend, backend, CLI, workers) and outlines how each one boots the app), and 13 more\n- **Commands** (27): `blueprint-create` (Create a complete product blueprint from the product foundation), `corpus-mine` (Mine the Waves artifact corpus — read every logbook's analyses across waves/projects, surface recurring findings, most-violated rules, most-omitted…), `cost` (Render the Waves cost report from the co-located cost.json files — token cost (cache vs normal) and frozen…), `diverged-work-create` (Capture a small unit of divergent work that surfaced mid-flight (during design or testing) as a diverged_work artifact…), `feasibility-analyze` (Pre-blueprint feasibility and market analysis with Monte Carlo and Bayesian projections), `foundation-create` (Compact feasibility analysis into validated facts for blueprint creation), `logbook-create` (Create a new development logbook for a ticket/task with structured objectives, autonomous design resolution, code tracing, UI detection,…), `logbook-update` (Update an existing logbook with progress entries, objective status changes, new objectives, and reminders), and 19 more\n- **Hooks** (5): `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `UserPromptExpansion`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install waves-exovian@claude-community` from `exovian-developments/waves-cowork-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
